n Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T15:01:34-08:00","id":8386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions?p=8370#post8370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies for making you repost that, I should've seen it in the first post.<br /> <br /> This is an interesting one, has anyone thought about converting the Norvegi and Bloodworking to fit the new way Disciplines work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a problem. <br /> <br /> Bloodworking would require a massive re-envisioning, as everything it currently does can be replicated with Protean. And I wouldn't want to jeopardize Protean by removing adaptation options like quills and armor just to enable a different discipline. At best I think Bloodworking might be reasonable as a set of Bloodline specific Protean devotions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T15:22:38-08:00","id":8399,"title":"","content":"That makes sense. I think they could have Protean pretty easily, but the most essential thing would be how they feed. Would that just be a Protean 2 Devotion? I'd be concerned if they couldn't feed from the Get go. Is there anything to represent their not having fangs or feeding the way they do using the new rules?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T15:29:02-08:00","id":8404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions?p=8399#post8399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes sense. I think they could have Protean pretty easily, but the most essential thing would be how they feed. Would that just be a Protean 2 Devotion? I'd be concerned if they couldn't feed from the Get go. Is there anything to represent their not having fangs or feeding the way they do using the new rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>A vampire can actually feed through Protean 1, though not in the normal sense of finding prey and biting it. They'd have to find places where blood was likely to flow and merge with the earth there, sucking up the drippings. It wouldn't be a pleasant way to eat, but then again that might fit them nicely. Then you could give them a 1 exp Protean devotion that lets them suck up blood just by touching it, which transitions nicely a Norvegi growing claws, slashing people and absorbing the blood through his talons.<br /> <br /> Edit: And now I have an idea. Might post something a little later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 11-11-2013, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T16:11:26-08:00","id":8440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions?p=5948#post5948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see Obtenebration that is more like it is supposed to be in Requiem, not tacking on old Obtenebration into new.<br /> <br /> I wanna see it able to fight spirits before the fifth dot. People who do revisions of it seem to forget its purpose and default back to the Masquerade disciplines concept. That isn't what Obtenebration is about anymore. Its the Discipline of the Khaibit, vampires who fight ghosts and spirits. The first level grants them the capability to see said spirits, and the fifth dot lets them fight them. Everything else in between really has little to do with it except for using 2-3 to help make it dark enough to see the spirits.<br /> <br /> I love the concept of using shadows to fight spirits, I just would like to see this reflected in the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I, too, would love to see Obtenebration get a rewrite that (while not making it horrifically game-breaking) would make it a more overtly-practical tool with regard to the Khaibits' ancient role as combatants in a war against spirits and other <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/EldritchAbomination\" target=\"_blank\">eldritch abominations</a> (some of which may be ethereal, some of which may be corporeal, and some being half-and-half in the same manner as the Uratha).<br /> FWIW, what I would propose is:<ul><li>The as-written Requiem versions of <i>Night Sight</i> and <i>Pulse of the Invisible</i> (Blood Tenebrous 1) are combined into a single ability and become the proposed Innate/Passive Ability.</li> <li>The as-written Requiem versions of <i>Shadow Play</i> and <i>Shroud of Night</i> are each &quot;downgraded&quot; by one dot, to respectively become the new Level 1 and 2 powers; they are useful for the purposes of stealth, distraction, and deception (and entertaining guests, for the more modern servant-oriented Khaibit).</li> <li>The proposed Level 3 power being something of a hybrid of the Masquerade versions of <i>Nightshades</i> (&quot;Create temporary objects made of shadow&quot;) and <i>Inner Darkness</i> (&quot;Drawn the shadow into yourself to gain great power&quot;) that allows the Khaibit to imbue material tools and weapons with shadow/darkness that grants said tool or weapon the ability to affect ethereal entities (e.g. a rope or set of handcuffs imbued with shadow/darkness can bind a ghost or spirit just as well they can a mortal, while a material blade that is imbued with shadow/darkness can damage a ghost or spirit as well as a mortal), as well as allowing stand-alone shadows/darkness manipulated or created by the proposed Level 2 power to affect <u>only</u> ethereal entities (e.g. trap one or more ghosts or spirits inside a box or dome composed of shadow/darkness, or cut them with a blade composed completely of shadow/darkness, etc).</li> <li>The as-written Requiem versions of <i>Perambulam in Tenebris</i> and <i>Shadow Form</i> remain in place as the Level 4 and 5 powers.</li> <li>A Devotion that builds on the proposed Level 3 power, allowing stand-alone shadows/darkness manipulated or created by the Level 2 power to affect corporeal entities in the same way that the proposed Level 3 power allows stand-alone shadows/darkness to affect ethereal entities (e.g. the Devotion would allow the Khaibit to trap one or more corporeal persons inside a box or dome composed of shadow/darkness, or damage said persons with a blade composed completely of shadow/darkness, use shadows to form weak barriers against physical attacks (in the same manner as Mage's &quot;Summon Shadows&quot; spell), etc).</li> </ul><br /> FWIW, this is based on my personal view of the ancient Khaibit as something of &quot;a vampiric rendition of the <a href=\"http://babylon5.wikia.com/wiki/Anla%27Shok\" target=\"_blank\">Anla'shok/&quot;Rangers&quot;</a> from <i>Babylon 5</i>&quot;: &quot;sentries and watchers, looking for the signs and collecting information quietly from their havens and from returning travelers and friendly sources in other domains, watching and waiting for the night when the denizens of the Greater Darkness - horrors beyond imagination which originate outside the ken of this plane of existence - return&quot;.<br /> I can easily imagine the ancient Khaibit having the same credo as the Rangers: &quot;We walk in the dark places no others will enter. We stand on the bridge and no one may pass. We live for the One, we die for the One.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It also makes Obtenebration somewhat more comparable to the shadow-oriented spells of the Arcanum of Death, practiced primarily by the Moros mages (and all found in the MtA Core book).<ul><li><i>Shadow Sculpting</i> (*) - (Covert) Shape or strengthen shadows</li> <li><i>Animate Shadows</i> (**) - (Vulgar) Compel shadows to move, even to an unnatural place</li> <li><i>Summon Shadows</i> (***) - (Vulgar) Create shadows from nothing; provide shadows with material properties</li> <li><i>Shadow Flesh</i> (****) - (Vulgar) Become a shadow. Requires Life 4, Optional Matter 4</li> </ul><br /> The combination of these spells with <i>Grim Sight</i> (the Death version of Mage Sight) and <i>Speak with the Dead</i> (allows the Mage to detect and converse with ghosts) effectively covers the same ground as the original VtR version of Obtenebration, and (IMO) serves as a reasionable point of comparison for where a rewritten Obtenebration could go without getting too out-of-hand/game-breaking.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?<br /> <br /> (P.S.: By contrast, VtM/Lasombra Obtenebration apparently allowed people to throw cars at each other with shadow-tendrils, defend oneself with shadow-armor and shadow-shields, perforate each other with shadow-lances, and so on; it sounds like one was basically <a href=\"http://fma.wikia.com/wiki/Pride#Powers_and_Abilities\" target=\"_blank\">Pride</a> from <i>Fullmetal Alchemist</i> (manga/<i>Brotherhood</i>)?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/212-stormbringer","name":"Stormbringer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T16:38:11-08:00","id":8460,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:21px\"><u>Bloodworking</u></span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Fingertongue \u2022</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cost: None<br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> Action: None<br /> Duration: Permanent</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Whenever the Norvegi comes in physical contact with blood she may consume it straight through her flesh, following the same rules and restrictions for feeding found in Protean 1. She may consume up to her Blood Potency in Vitae in this manner every action. The Norvegi use this method to feed from victims, either by draining directly from an open wound or picking up blood that has splattered on the ground (as a related note, many Norvegi travel bare foot). </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Hemophilia \u2022\u2022</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cost: 1 Vitae</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dice Pool: None</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Action: Instant for held weapons, Reflexive for natural weapons.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Duration: Scene</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">To better enable feeding Norvegi evolve a unique poison that she can secrete onto weapons, both natural (like Protean Claws) and artificial. Anyone who takes lethal damage from a poisoned attack must immediately roll Stamina + Supernatural Advantage, penalized by the Norvegi\u2019s Bloodworking dots or begin to bleed out. Stemming this blood loss is difficult, requiring an Intelligence + Medicine roll, difficulty 4. The undead and other bloodless lifeforms are unaffected by this poison.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Red Crafts \u2022\u2022\u2022</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cost: 1 Vitae</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dice Pool: Manipulation + Crafts + Bloodworking</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Action: Extended, target: size successes, one action per roll</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Duration: Scene</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Adding a single drop of Vitae into a pool of blood the Norvegi empowers the blood, causing it to shift and roil as if it was alive. While the blood is in this state the Norvegi can craft it, giving the red mass whatever form she pleases. She can create with the blood any simple object with a size no greater than the amount of vitae that blood pool would yield (if consumed by a BP 1 Neonate) or her Blood Potency, whichever is lower. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Creations are restricted to simple objects with no moving parts of electrical elements. Crafts are weak, with a durability of 1 regardless of potency, but flow back together when damaged. Weapons created in this manner are considered natural for the purposes of Hemophilia. Blood armor provides 1/0 soak, and blood cover only provides half its normal reduction against firearms. Finally, direct exposure to fire destroys crafted blood, evaporating it instantly.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Bloodflow \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cost: 2 Vitae, 1 Willpower</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dice Pool: Manipulation + Larceny + Bloodworking</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Action: Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Duration: Successes Actions</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">With a hiss like a snake and a roar from her beast the Norvegi calls to the blood around her, in and out of veins, beckoning it to her side. For a number of actions equal to her successes all blood within the Norvegi\u2019s [Blood Potency * 10] yards flows to her. Any living creature with open wounds must immediately roll Stamina + Supernatural Advantage or begin to bleed out. Anything that is already bleeding out doubles its rate of blood loss. The Norvegi may choose each action how much blood she consumes (up to her Blood Potency limit) and how much simply pools around her for use with other Norvegi powers.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Bloodform \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cost: 3 Vitae, 1 Willpower</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dice Pool: None</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Action: Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Duration: Indefinite</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Slashing her throat and wrists the Norvegi evacuates all Vitae from her body, taking her consciousness with it. She becomes a being of pure blood, leaving her husk of a body behind. While in this form the Norvegi retains all her physical attributes, powers, and ability to feed, though she loses the ability to speak save through gurgling. Her liquid form can flow easily through cracks and holes, making her impossible to grapple or restrain. She is also essentially invulnerable, only fire and sunlight can harm her (with storyteller permission other methods, like freezing, may be effective). </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Norvegi may retain this form indefinitely, but not without risk. Every scene in which the Norvegi retains this state consumes an point of Vitae. This is cumulative, first scene she loses one, second two, third three for a total of six Vitae lost. This will continue until the Norvegi returns to her body, or run out of Vitae completely. A Norvegi who does run out of Vitae in this form suffers final death, her mind and soul evaporating. Therefore Norvegi must be careful not to let others find her helpless body, lest they destroy it and doom her.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 11-11-2013, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T16:50:31-08:00","id":8466,"title":"","content":"That is very different but very excellent, and a fascinating way to handle the Norvegi. This version of Bloodworking makes me imagine the Norvegi as being a significantly divergent Bloodline, which is very cool.<br /> <br /> I feel like the poison is evocative of their assassin role given the fiction, but I'm wondering if there's anywhere else that can be evoked?<br /> <br /> Also, does their method of feeding dilute Vitae enough to prevent blood bonds a la Unmarked Grave?<br /> <br /> Finally, I appreciate Crafts there and I can get behind Larceny, but I wonder if Manipulation is the most suitable attribute. Why not Wits or Dexterity?<br /> <br /> Any chance you'll give us the Devotions too? This is seriously awesome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T17:12:20-08:00","id":8478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions?p=8466#post8466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is very different but very excellent, and a fascinating way to handle the Norvegi. This version of Bloodworking makes me imagine the Norvegi as being a significantly divergent Bloodline, which is very cool.<br /> <br /> I feel like the poison is evocative of their assassin role given the fiction, but I'm wondering if there's anywhere else that can be evoked?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly the mental image I began with was <b><a href=\"http://i137.photobucket.com/albums/q217/Taliesin_ttlg/spiderman/spiderman_morbius.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a></b>, and the image I ended with was<b> <a href=\"http://www.dvdtalk.com/reviews/images/reviews/197/full/1353164544_1.png\" target=\"_blank\">this</a></b>. So I wasn't really working from the fiction. But forming weapons from nothing and slipping through cracks as a red liquid monstrosity both seem pretty assassin-y to me. Hell, the entire discipline is themed around exsanguination.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions?p=8466#post8466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, does their method of feeding dilute Vitae enough to prevent blood bonds a la Unmarked Grave?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, good point. Let me think on that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions?p=8466#post8466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, I appreciate Crafts there and I can get behind Larceny, but I wonder if Manipulation is the most suitable attribute. Why not Wits or Dexterity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Manipulation doesn't get enough love, so I used Manipulation. Dexterity also works, though I don't really see Wits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions?p=8466#post8466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any chance you'll give us the Devotions too? This is seriously awesome!</div> </div> </div> </div>If I think of any, though at that point I'd throw them into a Google doc and post that up. <hr />On a related note, this thread really needs a hub post. A lot of good homebrew is getting buried in pages where it will never again be found. If Thorbes or Leetsepeak would be willing to edit their initial post this thread would become a lot more accessible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T17:27:13-08:00","id":8487,"title":"","content":"That's a good point on the assassin bit. I guess it's a bit of a happy coincidence that it turned out to be as evocative as it was before! Nicely done.<br /> <br /> I was going with Wits being quick/intuitive thinking to craft a weapon, but I understand the desire to give Manipulation greater utility, my concern was minding the assassin thing they've got going on that something like that might be out of place.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to imagine the mental reasoning why the Devotions could work to get some of the powers that the old Discipline had. I'm thinking there could be one that serves a dual purpose, most likely between Protean 2 and Bloodworking 3 which coaxes the Blood to flow out and uses the power of the Beast to shape them into weapons. I really like the image of Blood Claws, but they'd probably need a special purpose<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">differentiate them mechanically from the claws you can get from Protean 2 or 4. Maybe it'll start causing the target to bleed out? Maybe they absorb Vitae? Cool possibilities, there. </span></span><br /> <br /> Maybe with Protean 4 and Bloodworking 3, you can get the ranged attack from the original Bloodworking, where it's a similar principle, but you can manifest the unnatural power of the beast to launch some kind of blood spike at your target.<br /> <br /> Also for a point of clarity, how do you calculate the Blood being absorbed by the 4th dot? Would you treat the amount of blood as being equal to 1 Vitae per lethal damage from the attack + bleeding out?<br /> <br /> I'm trying to think of any other ones. Maybe a Devotion between Bloodworking 2 and Resilience for excreting a layer of bloody sweat which hardens like armor? Could be cool.<br /> <br /> Finally, given the crossover between Protean, would you still consider these guys good as a Mekhet Bloodline? I'm thinking it might be interesting to make them a Gangrel Bloodline, myself. Not *just* because of Protean. I feel like they could help present an assassin type for the Gangrel as well.<br /> <br /> Can't stress enough how excellent I think this version of Bloodworking is. Hats off to you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T20:00:26-08:00","id":8568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions?p=8487#post8487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to imagine the mental reasoning why the Devotions could work to get some of the powers that the old Discipline had. I'm thinking there could be one that serves a dual purpose, most likely between Protean 2 and Bloodworking 3 which coaxes the Blood to flow out and uses the power of the Beast to shape them into weapons. I really like the image of Blood Claws, but they'd probably need a special purpose differentiate them mechanically from the claws you can get from Protean 2 or 4. Maybe it'll start causing the target to bleed out? Maybe they absorb Vitae? Cool possibilities, there.<br /> <br /> Maybe with Protean 4 and Bloodworking 3, you can get the ranged attack from the original Bloodworking, where it's a similar principle, but you can manifest the unnatural power of the beast to launch some kind of blood spike at your target.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to think of any other ones. Maybe a Devotion between Bloodworking 2 and Resilience for excreting a layer of bloody sweat which hardens like armor? Could be cool.<br /> <br /> Finally, given the crossover between Protean, would you still consider these guys good as a Mekhet Bloodline? I'm thinking it might be interesting to make them a Gangrel Bloodline, myself. Not *just* because of Protean. I feel like they could help present an assassin type for the Gangrel as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAsk and ye shall receive. <u><b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xWnHbBWsgAbj86zsA7LvkXzwBbKxd2czYjXGXbII_7s/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Norvegi, converted to Gangrel, with a modified weakness, 4 devotions, and a merit.</a></b></u><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions?p=8487#post8487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also for a point of clarity, how do you calculate the Blood being absorbed by the 4th dot? Would you treat the amount of blood as being equal to 1 Vitae per lethal damage from the attack + bleeding out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bingo. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions?p=8487#post8487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't stress enough how excellent I think this version of Bloodworking is. Hats off to you!</div> </div> </div> </div>I just hope it sees use. Actually I basically already used on in my WWII arc, crazy scientist blood monster who exsanguinated people. Now he can have actual stats, yay!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T20:33:33-08:00","id":8576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions?p=8568#post8568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bAsk and ye shall receive. <u><b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xWnHbBWsgAbj86zsA7LvkXzwBbKxd2czYjXGXbII_7s/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Norvegi, converted to Gangrel, with a modified weakness, 4 devotions, and a merit.</a></b></u><br /> <br /> <br /> Bingo.<br /> <br /> <br /> I just hope it sees use. Actually I basically already used on in my WWII arc, crazy scientist blood monster who exsanguinated people. Now he can have actual stats, yay!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Awesome! Quick question on Bloodshot: Does that &quot;1 Lethal&quot; in the cost section indicate that the Norvegi suffers 1 Lethal damage to use the Devotion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T22:06:05-08:00","id":8613,"title":"","content":"So my latest VtR plot was going to feature a cult of blood bathers using strange rituals involving whole pools filled with blood, and... Well, now I need to add a Norvegi into the mix <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T22:25:31-08:00","id":8619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions?p=8576#post8576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awesome! Quick question on Bloodshot: Does that &quot;1 Lethal&quot; in the cost section indicate that the Norvegi suffers 1 Lethal damage to use the Devotion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yes. When using the mass attack variant it deals 1 lethal to the Norvegi herself, as she has to shred herself to use it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions?p=8613#post8613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So my latest VtR plot was going to feature a cult of blood bathers using strange rituals involving whole pools filled with blood, and... Well, now I need to add a Norvegi into the mix <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yay. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T00:15:47-08:00","id":8647,"title":"","content":"I like your rework of the Norvegi. But as it stands your Fingertongue and Bloodflow are almost identical to the second and fifth dot of the Phagia discipline of the Noctuku (Bloodlines the Chosen, p. 51). I'd probably use those two levels in a hypothetical rework of the Phagia discipline, but would then have to think of two new disciplines for the Norvegi that really set those two disciplines apart.<br /> <br /> EDIT: What is this Difficulty 4 you speak of under Hemophilia? :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T00:28:55-08:00","id":8654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions?p=8647#post8647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like your rework of the Norvegi. But as it stands your Fingertongue and Bloodflow are almost identical to the second and fifth dot of the Phagia discipline of the Noctuku (Bloodlines the Chosen, p. 51). I'd probably use those two levels in a hypothetical rework of the Phagia discipline, but would then have to think of two new disciplines for the Norvegi that really set those two disciplines apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not stepping on other disciplines when converting to B&amp;S is next to impossible. As is the existing disciplines step on each other, Bloodworking and Phagia especially. Compromising only ends up doing both disciplines a disservice. I wrote what I thought was a solid discipline, then added some devotions to replace lost powers. Glad you liked it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions?p=8647#post8647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: What is this Difficulty 4 you speak of under Hemophilia? :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Fiiiiine, rephrased.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T10:33:15-08:00","id":17796,"title":"","content":"I'm considering removing any Bloodline component from my version of Vicissitude and instead writing it as one of those apocryphal disciplines that anyone can learn if they can just find out how. Out of Clan cost, naturally. Hmm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T11:49:16-08:00","id":17835,"title":"","content":"One of the odd things I've done with the Masquerade Disciplines in the Conversion Guide is attach a blood potency requirement to them, making them the domain of elders due to their generally higher power-level.<br /> <br /> Just seemed a simple fix for my games though, since it meant I didn't have to put work into converting them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T12:36:53-08:00","id":17857,"title":"","content":"I just had a little epiphany as to why Manipulation is a cool choice for the Bloodworking stuff. It's coercing the Beast into controlling the Blood like so. I don't know if that sentiment was also a part of your choice Pen Dragon, but it makes a bit of sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T13:14:29-08:00","id":17885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions?p=17857#post17857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just had a little epiphany as to why Manipulation is a cool choice for the Bloodworking stuff. It's coercing the Beast into controlling the Blood like so. I don't know if that sentiment was also a part of your choice Pen Dragon, but it makes a bit of sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, lets go with that. You read my mind. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T20:28:20-08:00","id":18128,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">only had a crack at the first power so far but <br /> <br /> <u><b>Obtenebration</b></u> </span><br /> <br /> 1st Dot- <b>Tenebrous Vision</b><br /> <br /> <i>The Khabit in their ancient role of watchers in the darkness can see things that even kindred have cause to dread and fear. Ordinarily these phantasmal visions lurk on the periphery of a Khabit's perceptions but with effort can become focused and clear. By use of this power do they identify the invisible powers they were created to battle, and sometimes do the Khabits ancient enemies recognise them in turn. </i><br /> <br /> Cost: None or 1 Vitae<br /> <br /> Dice Pool: Wits + Occult + Obtenebration<br /> <br /> System: The character can see perfectly in complete darkness and never suffers penalties for acting in complete darkness or due to a lack of light source. As long as there is some shadow within the character's vicinity the character may reflexively roll the dice pool for this power to detect the presence of ephemeral entities, the use of any Influence or Numina used by such creatures, or if a location is affected by a Condition associated with an ephemeral entity. If successful the character receives the information as described through narrative terms and witnessed through menacing shadowy visions. <br /> <br /> By spending 1 Vitae the Khabit's eyes fill with an inky blackness that allows them to see any unmanifested ephemeral beings in their true forms as if they were corporeal for the rest of the scene, ephemeral entities possessing bodies may also be seen this way in a disturbing double vision overlayed one over another. Whilst seeing through these shadowed orbs it may be possible for certain beings to identify the Khabit as a threat to their inscrutable plans and begin to act accordingly, this should be handled at storyteller discretion and used for dramatic and thematic purposes to create conflict and story not to punish the player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T21:36:59-08:00","id":18160,"title":"","content":"So an update for Vicissitude: I've rewritten some of the fluff and cut out a number of extraneous features, removed the appendices and added in some Devotions. I'm currently in the process of figuring out the mechanics for the fifth dot, but definitely want to know how people think it's looking now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T14:11:43-08:00","id":22580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions?p=4920#post4920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always felt Blood Tenebrous worked much better as a Coil, being all trangressive and transcendent. Up till now the Coil system didn't really support it, but no more!<br /> <br /> In fact, I already wrote it. I wrote it even before I'd finished the three main coils. Much of the Coil design process was honed through adapting Blood Tenebrous. Since it's unlikely to get reprinted there's really no harm in sharing...though the Coil still needs a better name (If anyone has a proposal I'm all ears). Anyway, here for all to peruse, the tentatively named<b> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1aeMOY7Ph7BCyz0IwBA70aaflEo-dMi2VG5tAT5_rkS0/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Coil of Divinity</a></b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Love this stuff. I may use it in a game I run. Quick question, though. Can you use The Third Eye to notice spiritual possession, or just spirits floating around in Twilight?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1494-deranged-goblin","name":"Deranged Goblin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T13:09:42-08:00","id":23282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deranged Goblin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions?p=22580#post22580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Love this stuff. I may use it in a game I run. Quick question, though. Can you use The Third Eye to notice spiritual possession, or just spirits floating around in Twilight?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just tweaked the first dot to mesh better with the kindred template. Spirit sensing is now a factor of Kindred Senses, and thus based on Blood Potency. Spirits that have claimed hosts or been instilled into fetishes cannot be seen or heard, but can be smelled and their host sniffed out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T22:19:16-08:00","id":23542,"title":"","content":"My personal notes on how Obtenebration, as what I envisioned from Khaibit fluff, works out turns it into a blood sorcery discipline with rituals similar to the Abyssal magic from VtM Dark Ages, among others. The powers I would want tend to work better as less direct and immediate than most basic disciplines. I don't mind sacrificing immediate effects and require a little planning.<br /> <br /> In this case, I would put this new shadow sorcery somewhere in between Cruac and Theban, mainly because it would have motifs of both. I see it as powered by a source similar to the Strix or wherever they came from. The sorcery would be corrupting, but deliberate. The power would truly despise vampires even more than the source of Cruac. Sorcerers would have to &quot;steal&quot; the power for their rituals by force of their will and learning rituals would require lengthy meditation. In other words, the rituals would use humanity caps from Cruac and willpower and sacrifices of Theban. The &quot;source&quot; would desire nothing less than to consume these blood sorcerers whole. In this way, the sacrifices would serve as a conduit for the destructive backlash of taking power from this &quot;source.&quot;<br /> <br /> I would give a nod to the old black magic by giving the sorcerers an interesting quirk. As part of their devil's bargain, when they would normally turn into draugr, they instead get &quot;swallowed up&quot; by the &quot;source.&quot; The only thing left behind is a bit of the beast, yellow eyes wrapped in shadows. That would be the third motif by the way, shadow/darkness. I view the &quot;source&quot; as darkness incarnate. As the Atlantean mages viewed darkness as a force itself not just an absence of light, the &quot;source&quot; is one such force.<br /> <br /> I haven't decided if I would prefer an alternative to using an object as a sacrifice or not. I'm leaning towards making the sorcery powerless in sunlight any more direct than during a cloudy day, alterations would revert, control would be lifted, no targeting anything basking in the light of the sun, protections fade and creations disappear. In addition, all the rituals would have to be cast in darkness or low light conditions to further limit the discipline.<br /> <br /> The darkness motif would color all the rituals with a basis in shadow and cold, ravenous hunger. Divination would work using the knowledge of shadows, limiting it to past and present, but the shadows could watch the sorcerer's back to impart some of the same bonuses as future sight. Raw destructive forces would feel cold and draining while they crushed and ripped apart a target, taking away bits and pieces as if they were disintegrated. The sorcerer's shadow would appear next to a target's shadow and &quot;force&quot; it to do the sorcerer's will. Anything that has it's shape changed would retain it's original shadow. Anything created would lack a shadow completely as it would be made of shadow. Some things might appear black and ephemeral while others might appear to be literally dark shadows. In the latter case, all light would be absorbed giving the appearance of the blackness of space without the stars. This would be a possible look for creatures. They would have no depth or, perhaps, it would be better to say they have infinite depth. They would seem to be only 2 dimensional like a normal shadow but not attached to or &quot;on&quot; anything, but the 2-D image would change as the viewer's perspective changed to show that they really aren't &quot;flat.&quot; The exception would be their eyes and teeth. I imagine something like &quot;God&quot; from Fullmetal Alchemist.<br /> <br /> I'm having a little trouble with whether or not to create a new Shadow Theme. The five basic themes do a pretty good job of covering almost all the powers I would want to impart either singly or in combination.<br /> <br /> I think sorcery should be able to mimic all the powers from both canon versions of Obtenebration. Additional powers I would want to include beyond what the 5 basic Themes provide would be Mage spells from the Arcana of Death (allowing for interaction with ghosts and shadow spells), Space (Pocket Realm, Safe Keeping, Teleportation, and Oubliette) and possibly some Spirit or even Prime. I'm not interested in vampire Ghostbusters or Spirit Police. I do want a discipline that allows for a fairly broad ability to interact on a basic level with the ephemeral. I would keep a prohibition on plane-hopping to the Underworld and Shadow. Technically, seeing ghosts and spirits would not be allowed with blood sorcery so that might need to be a Devotion, but I could live with that.<br /> <br /> Those are some of my thoughts on the subject, but I'm pretty well stuck there until I can get a good long look at Blood &amp; Smoke. I need to know more about the Strix mechanics before I can decide on Anti-Strix powers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T12:32:06-08:00","id":23895,"title":"","content":"A conversation with Epimetheus yesterday inspired me to convert Chimerstry over from cWoD. So <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uMT-yLyRAcLUtRuTUrpxVTroL4AnYfz4qhQ1AeWfNQM/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">here it is</a>, complete with a Ravnos Bloodline and a few Devotions.<br /> <br /> Forum version for those who don't like Gdocs:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:27px\">Ravnos</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Clan: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Daeva</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Bloodline Disciplines:</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><i><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Chimerstry</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">, Majesty, Nightmare, Obfuscate</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Bloodline Bane: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Glass Phantoms</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The body of a Ravnos is as fragile as her signature discipline, she cannot tolerate the same degree of punishment as other Kindred. Ravnos </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">do not </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">downgrade lethal damage to bashing. A Ravnos with Resilience can downgrade up to her Resilience dots in lethal each turn, but cannot downgrade Aggravated damage.</span></span></span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:21px\">Bloodline Discipline: Chimerstry</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Note</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Illusions created by Chimerstry are true mirages, not psychic attacks. They will confound cameras and even the most mentally resolute, but do not carry any inherent mental qualities. So while an illusion may be described as \u2018terrifying\u2019 it possesses no supernatural compulsion towards fear.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Ignis Fatuus \u2022</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cost: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">None</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dice Pool: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">None</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Action: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Duration: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Scene</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Ravnos can conjure mirages, illusions that confound the senses and appear real. At this level the illusions are limited, they can be no larger than her Blood Potency in size, and affect only a single sense. Illusions may be given slight animation, water could appear to flow or a computer screen to flicker, but will not react to interaction. If the creator is close by she can puppet her illusions, giving them a greater semblance of reality, but upon close physical inspection they are revealed as falsehoods. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Fata Morgana \u2022\u2022</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cost: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">1 Vitae</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dice Pool: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Wits + Subterfuge + Chimerstry</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Action: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">None, Improves Ignis Fatuus</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Duration: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Scene</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Fata Morgana improves the illusions created through Ignis Fatuus. By spending one point of vitae the Ravnos increases the potential size up to [Blood Potency + 5] and allows illusions to affect all five senses, though at this level they are not real enough to cause extreme pain. Simple interaction is not guaranteed to penetrate these illusions, instead investigators roll Wits + Investigation, penalized by the Ravnos\u2019s activation successes, to determine the illusion false. While near a Ravnos can puppet illusions convincingly enough to make illusory people or interactive machines.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Apparition \u2022\u2022\u2022</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cost: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">1 Vitae</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dice Pool: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">None, Improves Ignis Fatuus</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Action: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">None, Improves Ignis Fatuus</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Duration: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Blood Potency + Chimerstry Days</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Ravnos can now create illusions that endure in her absence. By spending a point of Vitae while using Ignis Fatuus she improves the discipline in the following ways:</span></span></span><ul><li>Illusions gain a duration of [Blood Potency + Chimerstry] days, though she may specify a shorter period if she likes.</li> <li>Illusions may be programmed to react and respond in certain ways. This takes time, a few seconds per direction. The Ravnos\u2019s player should describe in a few sentences how she wants the illusion to act and react. Illusions are unintelligent, so while this can be enough to create convincingly interactive machines, compelling human illusions remain beyond the Chimerstry\u2019s ability.</li> <li>Illusions may be given triggers that cause them to emerge or fade. As with programming this can be as simple or complex as desired, anywhere from \u201csomeone opens this door\u201d to \u201ca black man stands in this spot for exactly seven minutes on a Wednesday\u201d. As illusions are unintelligent subjective or non-obvious triggers will fail. So \u201cAn untrustworthy enemy enters\u201d would be right out, and \u201cSomeone named bob passes by\u201d would only trigger if Bob\u2019s name were spoken aloud as he passed.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dreamscape \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cost: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">1 Vitae, 1 Willpower</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dice Pool: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">None, Improves Ignis Fatuus</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Action: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">None, Improves Ignis Fatuus</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Duration: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Scene</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Growing in power the Ravnos dramatically increases the size and scope of her illusions. By spending a point of Vitae and a Willpower while activating Ignis Fatuus she may increases the size and complexity of the illusion ten fold. It can encompass a space of up to [Blood Potency * 10] yards (or [Blood Potency + 5]*10 when using Fata Morgana). Within that space the Ravnos can craft many illusions simultaneously, in conjunction with Fata Morgana and Apparition she could create an entire ballroom, complete with guests (albeit slightly robotic ones), music, and apparently edible food.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Gossamer Reality</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u2022</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cost: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">2 Vitae, 1 Willpower</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dice Pool: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">None, Improves Ignis Fatuus</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Action: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">None, Improves Ignis Fatuus</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Duration: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Scene</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">At the height of Chimerstry\u2019s power the Ravnos blurs the line between real and unreal, creating glamours that fool reality itself. By spending two Vitae and a point of willpower while creating an illusion the Ravnos invests it with physicality, it is for all intensive purposes exactly what it mimics. This has it\u2019s limits: </span></span></span><ul><li>Direct attacks roll [Wits + Subterfuge], resisted by Composure, with no weapon bonus regardless of their apparent magnitude. All attacks deal only bashing damage.</li> <li>Objects can be no more durable than her Blood Potency. Living Illusions have at most [Blood Potency] health, and use the Ravnos's Wits for all rolls, or Wits + [Appropriate Skill] if actively directed.</li> <li>Illusions are still restricted in size, even with Fata Morgana an explosive will destroy no more than a few yards of space.</li> <li>Illusions possess none of the supernatural properties of the things they mimic, an illusory fire will not deal aggravated damage to vampires (just bashing), nor will illusory iron cleave the defenses of a changeling.</li> </ul><hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:21px\">Devotions</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Horrid Reality (Chimerstry 4, Nightmare 4)</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cost: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">3 Vitae</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dice Pool: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Wits + Subterfuge + Chimerstry vs Resolve + Blood Potency</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Action: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Duration:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Scene</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Ravnos plunges her victim into a world of total illusion. She takes total control over all his senses and may dictate freely what he sees and experiences. As with all Nightmare powers this experience cannot be a pleasurable one, no matter how the Ravnos presents it the world the victim sees with bear an eerie tint. Normally this requires the Ravnos touch her victim on either the head or neck, but if the Ravnos has Dread Presence active she may target anyone with whom she makes eye-contact. This lasts until the scene ends, the Ravnos is incapacitated, or the victim escapes the her presence.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">This Devotion Costs 4 Experiences to Learn</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Will-o\u2019-the-wisp (Chimerstry 1, Majesty 1)</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cost: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">1 Vitae</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dice Pool: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">None, Improves Ignis Fatuus</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Ravnos instills her illusions with the allure of majesty, drawing all eyes upon them. Anyone who sees an illusion created by this power is entranced and subtracts the Ravnos\u2019s Majesty dots from all Wits + Composure rolls to notice anything else.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">This Devotion Costs 1 Experience to Learn</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Fantasia (Chimerstry 5, Obfuscate 5)</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cost: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">None, Improves Oubliette</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Merging her powers of illusion the Ravnos creates a kingdom of absolute fantasy. She may use Chimerstry powers freely within her Oubliette, just as she can the powers of Obfuscate. More importantly all illusions, from both Chimerstry and Obfuscate, are treated as though enhanced through Gossamer Reality (at no extra cost). In this way the Ravnos claims absolute control over her dominion, able to freely create and alter whole structures of glamour.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">This Devotion Costs 6 Experiences to Learn</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://f